  "formulas": "# BEV skills soft-target descriptive supplement\n\nFrozen for this CPU computation on 2026-11-04, before inspecting its metric outputs. This is post-inference descriptive supplementary analysis, not pre-inference preregistration. Existing TEST prompts, model outputs, population, hard-label results and selection thresholds remain unchanged; no optimization/selection authority is created.\n\nPopulation: source skills/test.parquet, 6,755 rows /10,316 questions; include exactly all 1,280 questions carrying label_probs per model (choice280, Noul659, score341). Join by original flattened index plus qid, state, instructions, criteria/order, hard label and request identity. Preserve duplicate requests and null limitations. No hard-only target is converted into a soft target.\n\nLet q be source label_probs in source criterion order, and p be stable softmax of the full stored candidate logit vector. No temperature fitting or clipping; no target renormalization. Require finite probabilities in[0,1] and sum(q) within1e-5 of1, report maximum deviation. Noul order is true/false, corresponding to Yes/No. Candidate subsets may have different K; report by original question type rather than one pooled headline.\n\nTVD=sum|p-q|/2; vector Brier=sum(p-q)^2; soft CE=-sum(q*log p), natural logarithm; human agreement=q[argmax p]. For Noul additionally scalar Brier=(p_true-q_true)^2, separately named; its relation to vector Brier is checked. For score only: normalized soft RPS=sum over thresholds0..K-2 of(CDFp-CDFq)^2/(K-1). K>=2 required. Hard accuracy on the soft-present subset is a separately labelled diagnostic. ECE is not introduced as a soft-target metric.\n\nAll means are question-weighted within each type, no cross-dataset average. Report type n, distribution of K, qid groups, per-qid n<30 and exact0/1 hard-accuracy/constant-prediction flags. Constant prediction indices are descriptive behavior diagnostics, not proof of semantic failure; shared index across different qids is not a shared semantic class. Type/source target overlap and pretraining disjointness are not newly established.\n\nAudit every stored record's commitment, input/contract/model identity and label-logit arithmetic. Numerical tolerance1e-11 absolute for logprobs,1e-10 for formula identities; source values remain unchanged. Existing successful lifecycle/physical releases are verified on175. Model forward kernels/full vocabulary are not recomputed. This is not publisher-native probability scorer equivalence or a training gain.\n",
